            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Dianemwj"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was wonderful. I blanched the peaches briefly in boiling water to make them easier to peel. I pureed the strawberries by themselves first, then pressed them through a sieve to remove the seeds (DH doesn't like the seeds). I used a bit more strawberries than the recipe called for, probably closer to 2 cups, but I lost some of them by sieving them. The sorbet came out great. I love sorbet and now I won't have to spend a fortune for it at the grocery store. Thanks Austin!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "My Hot Southern Mess"
            },
            "reviewBody": "First and Formost, I made this recipe as written. Like many other reviewers, I agree that orange juice really overpowers everything. The flavor wasn't horrible just not what I was looking for. The second issue is this sorbet is not a save for later sorbet, it hardens to a rock solid mixed fruit ice cube... the mix would be good as a popsicle though.",
            "datePublished": "2021-07-19T19:36:34.010Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Aiko Bethea"
            },
            "reviewBody": "As other reviewers stated, the OJ really overpowered the taste. Also, don't know if the brown sugar really added anything- standard sugar would work just as well.",
            "datePublished": "2012-09-20T18:08:20.030Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kay Lemay"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious. Tastes like frozen summer. I have a ton of fresh-frozen peaches in the freezer, and I'll be making this all winter.",
            "datePublished": "2012-09-08T18:50:07.710Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
